invariant: INV-17
file: widemul.h
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: widemul_p256_point_affine no longer calls p256_wide_wipe_below
  after the wide call. Every object that call names is still wiped, so
  the vectors and the residue checks on arm64 pass: what stays is
  whatever the compiler spilled of the coordinates of a shared point and
  the inverse of its Z, in the frames under the dispatcher's caller.
  bin/p256_equiv_test calls each dispatcher over a painted stack and
  requires zero where the wipe's array lay.

--- old
        uint32_t finite = p256_wide_point_affine(x, y, a);
        p256_wide_wipe_below();
--- new
        uint32_t finite = p256_wide_point_affine(x, y, a);
